course: dictionary
lesson: 7176
title: Keeping going: perseverance
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Perseverance is a noun. It means keeping on trying to do something even when it is hard, or when you fail at first. Say it slowly: per-se-VEER-ance.
explain: «Perseverance means keeping going when things are difficult.» This sentence gives you the meaning in plain words. Look for clue words like difficult, hard or fail, because they tell you the person is facing problems.
explain: The clues can also come from a longer sentence. «Good rules protect people... self-control and perseverance, managing your wants and keeping going when it is hard, help you do the right thing day after day.» The words after the comma explain perseverance for you.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "Keeping going when it is hard helps you do the right thing day after day" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Perseverance is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say «show perseverance», not «perseverances».
fact: «Perseverance pays off» means that keeping going usually brings a good result in the end.
fact: In school, perseverance is a learning value: practise reading, keep going with tricky maths, and don't give up.
fact: In church teaching, perseverance means keeping faith through hard times.
fact: Perseverance is also the name of a rover on Mars, which has sealed rock samples in tubes.
exercise: «Perseverance means keeping going when things are difficult.» What does perseverance mean? | Sleeping in on a school day | Being very quick at running | *Keeping on trying even when it is hard | Giving up as soon as something is hard
exercise: Which choice shows perseverance? | *Ben tries the tricky maths sum again after getting it wrong | Ben copies the answer and forgets it | Ben throws his pencil down and stops | Ben hides his book so nobody can see it
exercise: «Good rules protect people... self-control and perseverance, managing your wants and keeping going when it is hard, help you do the right thing day after day.» Find and copy the two words that name qualities that help you do the right thing. | protect people | good rules | *self-control and perseverance | day after day
test: What does «perseverance pays off» suggest? | *Keep going, and it usually brings a good result | Stop trying when it gets hard | Money is always given to you for free | Only lucky people can win
test: Which sentence uses perseverance correctly? | *Nina showed perseverance by practising her reading every night for a month | Nina showed perseverance by falling asleep in the lesson | Nina showed perseverance by quitting after one try
exam: Which sentence is the best definition of perseverance? | Perseverance is a type of food eaten at breakfast | Perseverance is a loud noise made by a machine | *Perseverance is keeping going when things are hard, or after you fail at first
